ling in a talk with drake  that he meant himself when he said a  certain person only had one percent  chance of survival he actually predicted  kaido's defeat how crazy is that but  didn't commit another betrayal because  of his pride and i gotta say i kind of  respect that he's not like apoo where a  pooh will switch sides as many times as  you allow him to cool to catch up with  the supernova here and again i'm  guessing hawkins will survive into the  future so that one percent chance of  survival is kind of a lesson to not just  live based off of probability because if  luffy did that he definitely would not  have gotten as far as he did then seven  days pass no chance anyone can argue  that the fight is not over if kaido  hasn't come back to finish the fight in  seven days so even more so than last  time the identity of luffy as a yonko  killer ayanko destroyer or ayanko  defeater is settling in we get to see  progress made in the land of wano which  is a nice touch i'm looking forward to  seeing the exact specifics for what kind  of progress i appreciate the fact that  it's not just like okay let's save this  place leave and hope they figure it out  we actually get to see some progress  before we go which makes sense  considering how long we've been in wano  now we need some more payoff and to see  how much of a difference luffy's made  apu and inby seem to have made up with  the alliance and i'm not surprised appu  will make up with anybody hawkins's  refusal to switch sides easily stands  out all the more because someone as  fickle as apu is present in this arc i  wonder if oda will redeem apoo's  character by the end of the series but  so far he's definitely not a likable  dude then we got a big serious reveal  even though this is one piece and you  can never be sure that characters will  die some characters have died during the  war specifically ashrae and ezo died izo  died with his exchange against the cp0  agent maha obviously these aren't main  characters but it is sad to see  ashwanizo go i always thought izo was  very cool with his choice of weapons and  also the fact that he was associated  with the whitebeard pirates didn't hurt  either we then jumped to a few comedy  and fan service scenes that include  yamato and the straw hats cannot wait to  see those because this is super vague  here i'm wondering if luffy is fine now  or if he's still recovering same with  zoro and then we get the craziest bit of  news even though it's not necessarily  surprising we're shown that admiral  ryokugu aka green bull is on his way to  wano there was mention of admirals going  to wanna we knew the world government  were preparing to attack if luffy won  and in our one piece podcast we did  mention that they could easily be  accompanied with an admiral so it seems  like that has indeed happened we don't  know if only green bull has shown up or  if he came along with other admirals  like fujitora but nevertheless it is big  news because green bull is in all  likelihood zoro's father but before i  get into that it does say there's no  break next week so props to oda he's  been super consistent with these  chapters even though we are in a super  hype part of the story right now and he  could easily get away with taking more  breaks so we'll find out more about  green bull very soon so make sure you  are subscribed and hit that notification  bell so you don't miss it yo future goes  in here we got some new crazy updates of  this chapter from oro japan so it pretty  much says that we still don't see green  bull's face but he has a flower on his  back that he uses to push himself and  fly so there's speculation could this be  uh plant-based fruit as a lot of us  predicted that explains the you know not  being not having to eat for three years  thing the photosynthesis and all that  but it also raised the question could it  be some kind of mythical zone as well so  let me know what you think about that  crazy news we're also told that 